<title>USA: Sallie Mae to redeem 6.335 percent notes.</title>
<headline>Sallie Mae to redeem 6.335 percent notes.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sallie Mae said on Tuesday that it will redeem its 6.335 percent callable notes due August 12, 1999.</p>
<p>The security will be redeemed in its entirety on August 12, 1997, the financial service provider said in a statement.</p>
<p>The principal and final interest payment for the notes is due and payable on August 12, 1997, to holders of record at the close of business on August 11, 1997, it added.</p>
<p>The par amount of the notes is $50 million.</p>
<p>((New York Newsdesk 859-1610))</p>
